    "result_text": "The only remaining references are in the test file itself (intentional \u2014 it asserts those fields are gone). Everything is clean and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Removed the `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, and `membershipNumber` schema properties; added a single `memberId` string property with the new format's documentation.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (model) \u2014 Replaced the `customerCode` field/column (`customer_code`) and its accessors with `memberId` (`member_id`).\n\n3. **Schema SQL** (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) \u2014 Renamed the `customer_code` column to `member_id` (widened to `VARCHAR(32)` to fit the longer concatenated format plus any collision suffix).\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Replaced `customerCodeFor` with `memberIdFor`, which builds `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`: region from postcode (\u2192 `UNKNOWN` fallback), 2-digit fiscal year of the business-day-adjusted registration date, the existing 8-upper-hex HASH8 over (normalizedTelephone + lastName), and a Luhn `CHK` over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`. Added a `luhn` helper. Collision handling now dedups against existing `memberId`s. The audit log line and the structured `OwnerCreatedEvent` (and `primaryIdentifier`) now reference `memberId`.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Removed the `membershipNumber`/`checkDigit` mappings and methods. `memberId` auto-maps from the stored field. `fiscalYear` now derives from the `<FY>` segment of the memberId, and `locality` (and thus `ownerSegment`) from the `<REGION>` segment.\n\n**One notable pitfall I hit and fixed:** the new region-parsing helper was initially a `default String memberRegion(String)`. MapStruct treated it as a generic `String \u2192 String` mapping method and applied it to *every* string property in the generated mappers (nulling out telephone/address/postcode \u2192 400s). Making it a `private` interface method removed it from MapStruct's candidate methods while keeping it callable from the `default` methods that use it.\n\nThe test suite passes: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
